  data: {
    LLM: 'Six cards each. One round of bidding (no minimum, max 18); dealer may take the bid by equalling the highest bid. High bidder names trumps and must lead a trump to the first trick. If a trump is led, everyone must play a trump if able; if a non-trump is led, players may follow suit or trump. Trick won by highest trump, or highest card of led suit if no trumps. Winner of each trick leads to the next. Points are counted in order: high, low, jack, game, pedro, sancho.',
    Player: 'Six cards each. One round of bidding (no minimum, max 18); dealer may take the bid by equalling the highest bid. High bidder names trumps and must lead a trump to the first trick. If a trump is led, everyone must play a trump if able; if a non-trump is led, players may follow suit or trump. Trick won by highest trump, or highest card of led suit if no trumps. Winner of each trick leads to the next. Points are counted in order: high, low, jack, game, pedro, sancho.',
    objective: 'As a team or individually, be the first to reach 100 points by winning tricks containing scoring trumps: high (trump ace), low (trump two), jack (trump jack), game (trump ten), pedro (trump five, 5 points) and sancho (trump nine, 9 points). Total 18 points per deal. If the bid is made, score the points won; if the bid fails, the bidder loses the number of points bid.',
    gameplay: 'Six cards each. One round of bidding (no minimum, max 18); dealer may take the bid by equalling the highest bid. High bidder names trumps and must lead a trump to the first trick. If a trump is led, everyone must play a trump if able; if a non-trump is led, players may follow suit or trump. Trick won by highest trump, or highest card of led suit if no trumps. Winner of each trick leads to the next. Points are counted in order: high, low, jack, game, pedro, sancho.',
